      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that `dma_buf_create_sysfs_work_entry` is a union, and `dmabuf-\u003esysfs_entry` points at this allocation (after line 234).\n\nThere are two ways this could be freed:\n1) `file_count(dmabuf-\u003efile) \u003d\u003d 1` in `sysfs_add_workfn` in which case `kfree(dmabuf-\u003esysfs_entry)` frees the whole allocation.\n\n2) The non-error path during the destruction of `struct dmabuf` calls `dma_buf_stats_teardown` which does `kobject_put` on `dmabuf-\u003esysfs_entry-\u003ekobj`. That invokes `dma_buf_sysfs_release` which also does a `kfree` on the allocation.",
